123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The design of the Simple Budget Planner system was chosen to be simple, clear, and easy to use for university students and young employees who need help managing their finances. The user interface uses a clean layout so users can quickly add income, record expenses, and check their balance without confusion. This supports the target users identified in earlier phases.  )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The system was divided into three main parts: User Interface, Application Logic, and Database. This separation makes the system easier to develop, maintain, and improve in the future. The User Interface handles user interaction, the Application Logic performs calculations such as updating balances and checking budgets, while the Database stores all transactions securely.  )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (A mobile-friendly design was selected because many users prefer using smartphones to manage daily tasks. The system is also accessible on computers to provide flexibility for different users and devices.  )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Alerts and notifications were included in the design because they help users avoid overspending and stay within their monthly budget. This feature increases financial awareness and encourages better spending habits.  )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Basic authentication was selected to protect user data and privacy. Since the system is designed as a simple academic project, a basic login system is sufficient for the first version. More advanced security features can be added in future versions.  )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Finally, charts and summary reports were chosen to present financial information in a clear visual way. This helps users understand spending patterns and make better financial decisions.   )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
